{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.MeanInequalities","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.growth_gap_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.growth_gap_eq","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L122-L133","doc":"**The growth gap in closed form:** `q / ((q+q⁻¹)/2) = 2q²/(q²+1)`.\n\nThis is `1 + tanh (log q)`, the crossing discriminant carried by\n`QOU.Braiding.em_strong_ratio_tanh` — so the amount by which the like-pair\nchannels outgrow the p-n channel is `1 + δ_CP`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.pn_spectralRadius_lt_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.pn_spectralRadius_lt_pp","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L114-L120","doc":"**The p-n channel grows strictly slower than either like-pair channel.**\n\n`pp` and `nn` have spectral radius `q`; the balance-point p-n letter has\n`(q + q⁻¹)/2`, and AM-GM sandwiches it strictly between `1` and `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_lt_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_lt_self","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L101-L112","doc":"**The balance rate is strictly below `q`.**  `(q + q⁻¹)/2 < q` for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.one_lt_balance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.one_lt_balance","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L88-L99","doc":"**AM-GM.**  For `q > 1` the arithmetic mean of `q` and `q⁻¹` exceeds their\ngeometric mean `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_eigen_neg'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_eigen_neg'","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L84-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_eigen_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_eigen_pos","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L79-L82","doc":"**and both have magnitude `[2]_q/2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_eigen_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balance_eigen_neg","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L72-L77","doc":"**The balance point is where the two Hecke eigenvalues become exact\nnegatives.**  At `d = -h/2`, `(d + q) + (d - q⁻¹) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.halfQuantumDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.halfQuantumDim","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L69-L70","doc":"Half the quantum dimension of the fundamental, `[2]_q/2 = (q + q⁻¹)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balanceOffset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.balanceOffset","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The spectral balance offset `d = -h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PnBalancePointSpectralGap.heckeH","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PnBalancePointSpectralGap.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The Hecke `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}